    "body": "## Summary\r\n\r\nFlexAttention always builds a block-causal mask, which is causal within each\r\npacked document. This PR adds `FlexInnerAttention.Config.mask_type` so a model\r\ncan choose plain `\"causal\"` instead, matching the transformers backend's\r\n`attn_mask_type`.\r\n\r\n- `\"block_causal\"` is the default and keeps today's behavior.\r\n- `\"causal\"` doesn't depend on `positions`, so the mask is the same for every\r\n  batch. It's only correct when each sequence holds one document.\r\n\r\nA private `Config._causal_mask_mods(positions)` returns the selected mask_mods\r\nand raises `ValueError` on an unknown `mask_type`.\r\n`FlexInnerAttention.Config.build_attention_metadata` and\r\n`SlidingWindowFlexInnerAttention.Config.build_attention_metadata` use it instead\r\nof composing the masks inline; the sliding-window config inherits both the field\r\nand the method from its base. Masks are unchanged for every existing config.\r\n\r\n## Test plan\r\n\r\n`tests/unit_tests/cpu/models/common/test_flex_attention.py`: 6 passed\r\n(2 existing, 4 new).\r\n\r\n- **mask_mods.** On packed and single-document positions, `block_causal` is\r\n  causal ∧ same-document and `causal` is causal. The two agree on\r\n  single-document sequences, and `block_causal` is a strict subset of `causal`\r\n  on packed ones.\r\n- **Mask builders.** For both flex configs, the mask returned with `\"causal\"`\r\n  differs from the default `block_causal`, and the default is `\"block_causal\"`.\r\n  That covers both the full and sliding-window masks. It fails if either config\r\n  ignores `mask_type`.\r\n- **Guard.** An unknown `mask_type` raises `ValueError`.\r\n",
